Good point, thanks.  There are enough levels available that if
you end up with Stormbringer or whatever you can get to Basic
and have a really good melee weapon on tap.  Magicbane as the
primary wielded weapon (start out with Sting), Stormy or a
Brand as the secondary wielded weapon, a stack of highly
enchanted elven daggers in the machine gun quiver.

That makes it a question of strategy.  When is what enhanced.
If only the dagger skill is enhanced all the way up to Expert
before any of the spell schools, your wizard will be level
7 and still unadvanced in any spells.  I often get to 7 by
the time I get to mines end.  So for a wizard I'll seriously
consider advancing attack spells once before taking dagger
to expert.  A matter of tastes with no right answer.

Wizards can get to Expert at quarterstaff IIRC.  No quarterstaff
artififact is available to wizards without wishing for Quest
artifacts.  Unless you're going for a "squib" ascension without
using spells, I don't see the point on enhancing quarterstaff
anywhere near max.  Maybe not at all.  I'm inclined to switch
to dagger the first time a non-cursed one comes to hand when
I play wizards.


